The Rule of Commit Message

Author: SeaMc <sauthm_2015@qq.com>
Last Updated: November 7, 2026

==========================

Valsex uses the Conventional Commits specification.
The format for submitting information is (EBNF):

`<type>["("<scope>[{", "<other-scope>}]")"]["!"]":" <description>
["\n\n"<body>]["\n\n"(("BREAK CHANGING: " <break-msg>) |
<footer> | ("BREAK CHANGING: " <break-msg>) "\n" <footer>))]`

e.g. `
docs(chf)!: refactor the Readme and add docs/process/issues

BREAK CHANGING: Refactor the Readme
Close #120845
`

Scope Rule of Documentation Branch
----------------------------------

* chf: Community Health Files
* doc: Documentation Files (means `docs/`)

Scope Rule of Source Branch
---------------------------

* arch: Architecture Modified
-  Supporting a new archotecture;
-  Stop maintaining an architectures.

* make: Makefile Modified
